$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=g3t8  LOC_AFTER=?

* A congruence inside a finite product whose bound variable occurs in the antecedent: every set.mm product congruence has a ` $d ` that forbids it, so tools/congr.py proves the congruence under the closed antecedent ` ( f = G ) ` and carries it back with one ` syl ` .

s1::simpr |- ( ( A. i e. NN 1 <_ i /\ f = G ) -> f = G )
c1::id |- ( f = G -> f = G )
c2:c1:fveq2d |- ( f = G -> ( # ` f ) = ( # ` G ) )
c3:c2:oveq2d |- ( f = G -> ( 0 ..^ ( # ` f ) ) = ( 0 ..^ ( # ` G ) ) )
c4:c1:fveq1d |- ( f = G -> ( f ` i ) = ( G ` i ) )
c5:c4:adantr |- ( ( f = G /\ i e. ( 0 ..^ ( # ` f ) ) ) -> ( f ` i ) = ( G ` i ) )
c6:c3,c5:prodeq12dv |- ( f = G -> prod_ i e. ( 0 ..^ ( # ` f ) ) ( f ` i ) = prod_ i e. ( 0 ..^ ( # ` G ) ) ( G ` i ) )
qed:s1,c6:syl |- ( ( A. i e. NN 1 <_ i /\ f = G ) -> prod_ i e. ( 0 ..^ ( # ` f ) ) ( f ` i ) = prod_ i e. ( 0 ..^ ( # ` G ) ) ( G ` i ) )
$)
